@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Notice";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Learn how information is handled in the Safeline local demonstration and what to avoid entering while using the app.";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <nav class="page-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a asp-page="/Index">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Privacy notice</span></nav>
    <header class="content-page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">IMPORTANT INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy notice</h1><p>This page explains the data limitations of this Safeline demonstration.</p></header>
    <section class="content-panel"><h2>Demonstration only</h2><p>Safeline is a local demonstration for internal review, not a production service. Do not enter real passwords, financial account details, identity numbers, or other sensitive personal information.</p>
        <h2>Account and plan information</h2><p>When you use the demonstration account features, account details and information you add to your protection plan are handled by this app and its configured local database. How the app is hosted and configured may affect where that data is stored and who can access it.</p>
        <h2>Use test information</h2><p>Use fictional names, email addresses, and phone numbers when exploring the demo. Avoid reusing passwords from other services.</p>
        <h2>Questions and data removal</h2><p>If you are testing a locally hosted copy, contact the person responsible for that environment to ask how its database is managed or removed. Signed-in users can also use the account deletion option where available.</p>
    </section>
    <p class="mt-4"><a asp-page="/Index" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Back to home</a></p>
</div>
